{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>We have sinned</b> — And behold, this is the beginning of the response of this psalm, that he confesses his sin and the sin of his people; therefore: <b>we have sinned with our fathers</b>, in the manner of <i>and they shall confess their iniquity</i> (Leviticus 26:40)." "<b>and we have acted wickedly</b> — corresponding to <b>our transgressions</b>." "<b>and we have done wickedly</b> — It lacks [an object], like <i>the way we have sinned</i> or <i>our soul</i>, and <b>so have we acted wickedly</b>. Perhaps it is a participle."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 106, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:40.923172577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}